# .gitignore for the claude-klabauter published repo root.
#
# Shipped FROM `dist/klabauter-toplevel/` via the `claude-klabauter-publish-repo-toplevel`
# flat-mirror row (publish-targets.portable) -- see the sibling `.percolate-ignore` in this
# directory for why it moved here instead of staying an (never-authored) destination-native
# file. Fixes the unscanned-published-check noise measured live (499 findings, all
# `__pycache__/*.pyc`, on one real `claude-klabauter-publish-repo-toplevel` run): anything
# that runs Python inside a fresh clone of the published repo (pytest, a stray `python -m`)
# accumulates untracked bytecode-cache noise otherwise.

# --- Python build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# --- Coordinator working state, never OSS payload ---
# No publish row ships `state/` here. When it appears it is a stray session
# writing its own orientation cache or session-hierarchy JSON into the mirror
# (observed 2026-08-10 and again 2026-08-11) -- internal content that must not
# reach a public repo via a blanket `git add`.
state/

# Same class, two more strays observed 2026-08-15: a session's own `.claude/`
# scaffolding, and `Saved/ProjectRag/` -- a ~190MB example-retrieval-repo index (graph.db
# plus structural sqlite and its -shm/-wal siblings) left by someone indexing
# the mirror. Neither is OSS payload. Untracked-but-unignored is the worst of
# both here: it never publishes, but it does trip percolate-round's dirty-dest
# check, whose offered remedy (`--reconcile-dest=discard`) resets the mirror to
# HEAD and removes residue -- which would delete an expensive index this repo
# does not own and cannot regenerate.
.claude/
Saved/

# --- Editor / OS detritus ---
*.bak
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
